A||N||2||Bowtie||New to Fiero world, have some questions||||1||
Z||000000||Bowtie||12-06-1999||11:54 AM||||I'm looking at buying an '86 GT, what should I look for as far as mechanicals? Mileage is still unknown but the body and interior is mint and they are asking $3800, is that too much? It's an automatic and I know nothing about these tranny's. Are they any good, are they durable or would I be better suited looking for a 5-speed. I'm not going to be doing any major modding to this thing so I'm jsut curious as to whether the factory auto is good for just some intake and exhaust work and then a little beting. Thanks in advance.<BR>Guy||||reg||1
Z||000001||87GT||12-06-1999||02:27 PM||||Run...run for your life!!  No, I am just kidding.  That price sounds okay if the car is in really good shape.  Seems like a lot of people here at the forum have had problems with clutches, although I have yet to have any with mine.  Mine has the 5-Sp in it.  Just remember that these fine machines are 11-15 years of age and will want money spent on them from time to time.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||12-06-1999||02:29 PM||||Last thing first. The auto tranny holds up pretty well, of course any tranny will fail sooner or later after constant abuse. Sometimes they just plain wear out (auto and manual) even if driven easy. I have an auto in my V8 Batmobile.<P>Personally, $3800 for an 86 GT sounds a little high, unless it's a low mileage, well maintained car in excellent condition. On the other hand, it's only money and you can't take it with you. The asking price on a used car is generally fairly negotiable, so I'll hold off further judgement until we hear more about the car and price.||||reg||1
